

### Normal or Gaussian Probability Function

#### 26.2.1 Z(x)=\(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\,e^{-x^{2}/2}\)

\[Z(x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt = \int_{-\infty}^{x}Z(t)dt\]

\[Q(x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt = \int_{x}^{\infty}Z(t)dt\]

\[A(x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-x}^{x}e^{-x^{2}/2}dt = \int_{-x}^{x}Z(t)dt\]

\[P(x) + Q(x) = 1\]

\[P(-x) = Q(x)\]

\[A(x) = 2P(x) - 1\]

